    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds like a standard procedure, but let's look at the actual data. The sensor logs are very specific—the package showed zero impact or rough handling during the entire transit. Since the customer is already being aggressive, I'm worried they're just trying to score a free item. If we ask for photos, they'll probably just send something staged. Given that the logs basically prove the carrier isn't at fault, should we just deny the refund right now to save the cost?",
